<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9124" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνοδία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a road that is no road,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδὸν ἢ κυριώτερον εἰπεῖν ἀνοδίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.156
				</span></i>
			, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρήμην ἀνοδίαν ἑαντοῖς συντεμεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Chr.</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			; mostly in dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνοδίᾳ, ἀνοδίαις,</span>
			<i>through places with no roads,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				5.13.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.57.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				19.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.508d
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mar.</u>
				37
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>ascent,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνοδίαι καὶ στάσεις τοῦ ἡλίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Vett.Val.
					343.18
				</span></i>
			.</div>
